        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сын (syn) from Proto-Slavic synŭ — inherited from PIE suHnús, \"son\". Vasmer lists Lithuanian sūnùs, Sanskrit sūnú- and Gothic sunus, so English son is a cousin, and he links the word with a Sanskrit verb \"to give birth\"."
            }
          ]
        },
